<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclusions.

  Policy: a finding is fixed, not excluded. An entry is added here only when the finding
  is a verified false positive or an unavoidable consequence of an API we must use, and
  every entry carries a comment stating why. Keep matches as narrow as possible
  (class + bug pattern), never a whole package or a whole category.
-->
<FindBugsFilter xmlns="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0">
  <!--
    KinfoProc is a JNA Structure over the start of macOS's struct kinfo_proc (ADR-0010). JNA writes
    its public fields by reflection when it reads the native memory, so SpotBugs sees them as never
    written; p_vmspace and p_sigacts are never read by Prism but must be declared, because their
    places give p_flag, p_stat and p_pid their offsets. An unavoidable consequence of mapping a
    native structure with JNA, which the milestone 8 review asked for instead of bare offsets.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="prism.srm.platform.macos.KinfoProc"/>
    <Bug pattern="UWF_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,NP_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,UUF_UNUSED_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD"/>
  </Match>
  <!--
    The Job Object structures of milestone 10 (JobObjectStructures, ADR-0002) are JNA Structures over
    JOBOBJECT_BASIC_LIMIT_INFORMATION, JOBOBJECT_EXTENDED_LIMIT_INFORMATION,
    JOBOBJECT_CPU_RATE_CONTROL_INFORMATION and JOBOBJECT_BASIC_ACCOUNTING_INFORMATION. JNA writes and
    reads their public fields by reflection around each call, and every documented field must be
    declared for the others to have their documented offsets, although Prism reads only a few of
    them. The same unavoidable consequence of mapping a native structure as for KinfoProc. Their
    fields keep the names of the documented C structures (ControlFlags, CpuRate, LimitFlags, ...), as
    jna-platform's own structures do (WinNT.IO_COUNTERS), so that each can be checked against
    Microsoft Learn by name: hence also NM_FIELD_NAMING_CONVENTION, for these classes only.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="~prism\.srm\.platform\.windows\.JobObjectStructures\$.*"/>
    <Bug pattern="UWF_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,NP_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,UUF_UNUSED_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,URF_UNREAD_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,NM_FIELD_NAMING_CONVENTION"/>
  </Match>
  <!--
    JnaSdBusApi.SdBusError (milestone 12, S3A) is a JNA Structure over libsystemd's sd_bus_error
    {const char *name; const char *message; int _need_free;} (systemd v255 src/systemd/sd-bus.h). sd_bus_call fills
    its fields in native memory and JNA copies them into the Java fields (Structure.read), so SpotBugs never sees a
    Java write: the fields are written by native code, not unwritten. _need_free keeps the C field name, which JNA
    needs to match the layout.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="prism.srm.platform.linux.JnaSdBusApi$SdBusError"/>
    <Bug pattern="UWF_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,NP_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,UUF_UNUSED_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,URF_UNREAD_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD,NM_FIELD_NAMING_CONVENTION"/>
  </Match>
  <!--
    HostPlatform.resourceLimiter() returns the one native limiter the composition root shares on
    purpose ("the same instance on every call"), as processController() does. SpotBugs reports
    EI_EXPOSE_REP only because ResourceLimiter gained clearOwned(LimitRecord) in milestone 12 (S1,
    the name the reviewed plan Rev 2.1 fixes): MutableClasses treats any method whose name starts with
    "clear" (also set, put, add, remove, ...) and does not return its own type as a setter, and so the
    interface as mutable state. Verified against spotbugs 4.10.4's MutableClasses.SETTER_LIKE_PREFIXES;
    nothing of HostPlatform's is exposed. Limited to this one method.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="prism.srm.platform.HostPlatform"/>
    <Method name="resourceLimiter"/>
    <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
  </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
